# Phase 18 P18-V01 `MqClientAdmin.deleteTopicInNameserver` — 2026-10-18T03:19:55Z

## Scope and source

- Continued on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`; the pinned Java
  oracle at `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq` remained read-only.
- Reconciled Java 5.5.1 `MqClientAdminImpl.deleteTopicInNameserver`: request
  code 216, direct NameServer address, `DeleteTopicFromNamesrvRequestHeader`,
  no body, null result on `SUCCESS`, and `MQClientException` with response
  code/remark otherwise.
- The Namesrv header has nullable `topic` and `clusterName` because
  `checkFields()` is a no-op. It inherits `ns`, `nsd`, `bname`, `oway`, and
  `lo`; inherited equality/hash only considers the four RPC base fields.

## Implementation

- Added the public Rust header, RPC-base equality semantics, nullable-field
  validation and typed-header inventory/cross-decode coverage, plus
